\fs22
\b Solo Maintainer Checklist — ED Pipeline (Gate-first, no-MLP)\b0\par
\par
\b Purpose\b0\par
Lean operating notes for a single maintainer. Keep the baseline stable, make small improvements, and validate quickly. No extra tooling required.\par
\par
\b Current baseline snapshot\b0\par
- Tag: \b gate_first_nomlp_baseline\b0\par
- Kernelspec: \b python3\b0\par
- Defaults: CONFIG[RUN\_UI]=False; CONFIG[RUN\_PIPELINE]=False\par
- Sanity status (at last freeze): ttl\_max\_ok=True; gates\_wired\_ok=True; bundle\_ok=True\par
\par
\b What not to change (invariants)\b0\par
- Single HL7 parsing path (\i parse\_hl7\_all\i0). \ul Do not\ulnone re-add parsing inside calculators/bundle.\par
- No I/O inside calculators or bundle; logging happens in pipeline cells only.\par
- Gate merger semantics: TTL=\b max\b0; priority=\b max\b0; order-preserving de-dup; next\_action=\b last non-empty\b0.\par
- Keep function names stable: \i merge\_gatepacks, gate\_engine, build\_labs\_norm, compute\_phase2\_scores, phase2\_bundle\i0.\par
- Paths remain CSV/dir semantics; notebook kernelspec = python3.\par
\par
\b Session workflow (reliable loop)\b0\par
1) Choose \b one\b0 small improvement (new gate or threshold tweak).\par
2) Run \b config/bootstrap\b0, then G1 (merger) + G2 (engine).\par
3) If editing Phase-2: run HL7 unified → Calc utils → Calcs A → Calcs B → Bundle B1–B3.\par
4) Run \b Triage Harness\b0 and \b Sanity Pack\b0 at the end. If green, publish; if red, undo the last change.\par
5) Update the handoff note only if thresholds or gates changed.\par
\par
\b Execution order (cells)\b0\par
- Minimal gate checks: CONFIG → G1 (merge) → G2 (engine) → Sanity.\par
- Bundle/HL7 checks: add HL7 unified → Calc utils → Calcs A → Calcs B → B1 → B2 → B3.\par
\par
\b Validation (must pass)\b0\par
- \b TTL\_MAX\_OK\b0: merger uses max per-gate TTL.\par
- \b GATES\_WIRED\_OK\b0: ICU capacity + BGA criticals produce expected gates/alerts.\par
- \b PHASE2\_BUNDLE\_SMOKE\_OK\b0: canonical HL7 → one-liners + scores return.\par
\par
\b Threshold governance (knobs)\b0\par
- ICU capacity: TH\_ICU\_CAP\_OK (default 0.15). Blocked: cap ≤ 0.0; Tight: 0.0 < cap < TH.\par
- BGA (venous): pH ≥ 7.50 (HIGH), pH > 7.55 (CRITICAL); K\super +\nosupersub: ≥ 6.5 (CRIT), ≥ 6.0 (HIGH), < 2.5 (CRIT);\par
  Na\super +\nosupersub: ≤ 125 (CRIT), outside 130–144 (DYSNATRAEMIA); Lactate ≥ 4.0 (CRIT).\par
- Overdue/alerts: last\_seen, since\_vitals\_min thresholds (exposed in UI when enabled).\par
\par
\b Ethics & scope guardrails\b0\par
- Exclude protected attributes from gates; use clinical signals only.\par
- Prefer systolic BP context over MAP unless arterial line exists.\par
- When venous BGA present, include pH / K / Na / lactate into gating.\par
\par
\b Data handling\b0\par
- Avoid storing PHI; use synthetic or minimized fields for testing.\par
- Event log is append-only; no PII.\par
\par
\b Release notes (3 bullets max)\b0\par
- What changed: \par
- Why it helps: \par
- How validated: which sanity probe(s) are green.\par
\par
\b Re-entry quick map (common failures → fixes)\b0\par
- NameError: \i merge\_gatepacks\i0 → run G1.\par
- NameError: \i gate\_engine\i0 → run G2 after G1.\par
- NameError: \i \_pick/\_bool/\_safe\_round\i0 → run Calc utils.\par
- calc\_qsoFA vs calc\_qsofa mismatch → alias once or normalize name in Calcs A.\par
- NameError: \i parse\_hl7\_all\i0 → run unified HL7 cell.\par
\par
\b File naming / slug\b0\par
- Use ASCII, hyphens, and date: \i gpt-gate-engine-ed-pipeline-YYYY-MM-DD.ipynb\i0.\par
- “Slug” = URL/file-safe label derived from a title (lowercase, hyphenated).\par
\par
\b MLP re-introduction (later, optional)\b0\par
- Gate-first remains arbiter; MLP may \b refine\b0 priorities but \ul never veto\ulnone safety gates.\par
- Calibrate probabilities (Platt/Isotonic) before using outputs; monitor drift.\par
\par
\b Time budget suggestion\b0\par
- 45–60 min per session: one change, run sanity, publish or roll back.\par
\par
\b Small templates\b0\par
\ul Release note\ulnone : What / Why / Validation.\par
\ul Incident review\ulnone : Summary (3 lines) → Timeline → Effects → Contributing factors → Fixes (owners/dates) → Prevention signals.\par
\par
\b Done when\b0\par
- All three sanity probes pass and no new gates regress.\par
\par
